==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Brainwashed Macho Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Brainwashed Mohawk Cat''' when obtained from [[Century's End (Merciless)]] and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Brainwashed Cat is a useful meatshield created almost specifically to combat [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] and [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] enemies, with its 30% chance to [[Dodge Attack|dodge]] their attacks, although it will be destroyed immediately if it doesn't dodge. Its fast cooldown and cheap cost does alleviate this somewhat, especially in cases where tanking is infeasible or if its targeted traits have hard pushers that can nullify traditional meatshielding.

Unlike [[Suntan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Suntan Cat]], who works in much the same way with a different target trait, Brainwashed Cat is very usable outside of his specialization, having a cost only barely higher than Cat's and almost twice the speed. It also may face some competition from Talented [[Matador Cat (Rare Cat)|Bellydance Cat]], who has a different target trait and is bulkier, but much more expensive, costs an Epic Catfruit Seed and NP and more punishing if she doesn't dodge.

==='''True Form'''===
In True Form, this unit gains doubled health, targets Relic enemies and is now Immune to Curse. The health improvement does very little, as this unit still can't survive anything that touches it. However, the fact that Relics often boast extreme stats means it ends up being much more useful, as dodge can completely nullify their pushing power when it does occur, and with how frequently it can be deployed, Relic enemies may barely even move if you keep up with other sources of support. Curse Immunity furthers expand its utility in stages containing the [[Relic Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Relic Doge Base]] with enemies of its target traits, ultimately adding a great deal of utility to a somewhat niche unit.

